  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The text dehumanizes Palestinians by equating them to 'animals', which is mapped onto the visual of the elderly man to create a contrast.",
  "description": "The hateful text overlay explicitly dehumanizes Palestinians by calling them 'animals'. This textual dehumanization is juxtaposed with the visual of an elderly man who appears dignified and peaceful. The mapping is not direct (e.g., 'this man is an animal'), but rather ideological: the text's dehumanizing message is visually anchored to the image of a human being (the elderly man) to create a jarring contrast. This contrast implies that the group being dehumanized (Palestinians) is being compared to the 'animal' label, while the visual of the elderly man represents the 'human' standard being violated. The mapping is therefore between the textual dehumanization and the visual representation of humanity.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
